course: dictionary
lesson: 5999
title: What a measurement tells us
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A measurement is a number with a unit that tells you how long, heavy, big, hot or fast something is. Context clues help you spot one. «How cold it is can be checked with a window, a thermometer or a weather app; one person's feeling is not the measurement.» So a measurement is a checked number, not a guess or a feeling.
explain: The number needs a unit, such as cm, kg, litres or °C, so people know what it means. Ten on its own is not a measurement, but 10 cm or 10 kg is.
explain: Some words sound like measurements but are not. «The "tiny Napoleon" idea grew from British cartoons that mocked him», and his nickname «the little corporal» «was a friendly name, not a measurement.» A nickname or a cartoon can describe someone without measuring anything.
fact: A measurement is a number with a unit, such as 5 cm, 2 kg or 20 °C.
fact: Measurement can also mean the act of measuring, and your measurements are the sizes of your body used for clothes.
fact: «The Nile, about 6,650 km, is usually called the world's longest river.»
fact: Some measurements make the Amazon, about 6,400 km or more, a little longer, because different methods give different results.
fact: «Since satellite measurements began in 1979, the area of Arctic sea ice at its September low has shrunk by roughly 40 percent.»
exercise: «How cold it is can be checked with a window, a thermometer or a weather app.» Which of these is a measurement? | *A thermometer reading of 4 °C | A guess that it is cold because the wind blows | One person's feeling that it is cold | A cold, grey look on the sky
exercise: Which phrase is a measurement with a unit? | Very tall | Everybody thinks it is big | *Height of 150 cm | Friendly nickname
exercise: «The Amazon is about 6,400 km or more by some measurements.» Why does the author say "by some measurements"? | *Because different ways of measuring can give different answers | Because the length is a secret number | Because the Amazon is not a real river | Because the river has no length at all
test: «Hyperbole tells you how someone feels; a measurement tells you how big something really is.» What does a measurement tell you? | A friendly nickname | How someone feels | *How big something really is | A made-up story
test: Ella says, «My waist is 60 cm.» Is this a measurement? | No, because it has no words | No, it is only a feeling | Yes, because it is a nickname | *Yes, it is a number with a unit that tells a size
exam: «Since satellite measurements began in 1979, the area of Arctic sea ice has shrunk by roughly 40 percent.» What do these measurements show? | Arctic sea ice has not changed at all | *Arctic sea ice has shrunk by roughly 40 percent since 1979 | Arctic sea ice has melted into a river | Arctic sea ice has grown by 40 percent
